orkspaces to any MCP-compatible AI agent, turning static documents into live knowledge infrastructure. Allows AI agents to query and use knowledge graphs from Notion without custom ETL pipelines.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n    \"category\": \"AI infrastructure\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Product Hunt\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\"If you're building AI agents, this immediately surfaces how MCP changes the integration game\", \"Your users' knowledge graphs become queryable context without custom ETL\"]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Latchkey\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.producthunt.com\",\n    \"description\": \"Credential layer for local AI agents that solves the security gap in local agent deployment by providing granular credential management. Offers reference architecture for credential isolation in production deployments.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n    \"category\": \"AI infrastructure\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Product Hunt\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\"Local agent security is underexplored; this offers a reference architecture that most production deployments currently lack\"]\n  }\n]"
